From cfaf72d08c0140718b28911f89aa64ceef6c8da1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 02:48:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] MFront rkCastem: Young modulus as stress error normalization
 factor

The variable `young`, when defined, is used as the stress error
normalization factor of the rkCastem algorithm, as stated in the release
notes of TFEL 4.1: the result of `checkVariable("young")` was discarded,
so that the stiffness tensor or the other choices were used instead, and
a behaviour whose Young modulus is only defined as a static variable was
refused ("no appropriate error normalization factor found"). The
previous commit (fb5c52bc5) wrongly stated that using it would change
existing behaviours: among the Runge-Kutta test behaviours of TFEL, only
OrthotropicCreep_rkCastem is affected, whose local variable `young` is
defined, for this purpose, as D(0,0), the value used before.

Also:
- checkVariable raises an error if the variable is defined for some
  modelling hypotheses only (the test could not fail);
- the two error messages about stress_error_normalization_factor were
  swapped.
---
 mfront/src/RungeKuttaCodeGeneratorBase.cxx | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/mfront/src/RungeKuttaCodeGeneratorBase.cxx b/mfront/src/RungeKuttaCodeGeneratorBase.cxx
index 3a06042c3..0e20ba521 100644
--- a/mfront/src/RungeKuttaCodeGeneratorBase.cxx
+++ b/mfront/src/RungeKuttaCodeGeneratorBase.cxx
@@ -1253,7 +1253,7 @@ namespace mfront {
     }
     //
     if (bd.isNameReserved("young")) {
-      checkVariable("young");
+      return checkVariable("young");
     }
     // look if the stiffness tensor shall be provided by the solver
     if (bd.getAttribute<bool>(BehaviourDescription::requiresStiffnessTensor,
